# suite-classification.data - Declarative unit/integration classification for every suite
# discovered by tests/run-all.sh. Adding a suite is a DATA EDIT here, never a documentation edit
# -- lint/lint-unit-integration-boundary.sh requires every discovered suite to have a row and
# fails loudly on an unclassified suite, so this file cannot silently drift out of sync with the
# corpus.
#
# SCOPE NOTE: this file is owned by, and physically lives under, the core extension, but its
# coverage is NOT core-only. In the DEPLOYED tree every extension's own scripts/tests/*.sh is
# merged flat into one shared .claude/scripts/tests/ directory (deploy-headless.sh's own
# per-extension merge), and that merged directory -- not any single extension's source-store
# tests/ tree -- is what tests/run-all.sh (gate 8) actually discovers and runs in production. A
# suite physically filed under a different extension (approvals/, lean/, literature/, ...) still
# needs a row here the moment it lands in that merged set; re-run against the deployed tree
# (lint-unit-integration-boundary.sh's default `--tests-dir` resolves to its own sibling
# ../tests/, which is core-only in the SOURCE STORE but the full merged set once deployed) before
# trusting this file complete.
#
# Format: one row per suite, TAB-separated, 3 fields: basename  class  reason
#   basename   The suite's own filename (e.g. "test-foo.sh"), matched against run-all.sh's own
#              discovered-suite basenames.
#   class      "unit" or "integration".
#     unit        -- must not spawn deploy-headless.sh, verify-deploy.sh, or (nested) run-all.sh.
#                    lint-unit-integration-boundary.sh enforces this mechanically; a suite
#                    reclassified to unit while still invoking one of those three is a lint
#                    failure, not a silent pass.
#     integration -- a full-system check wearing the test harness's clothing (spawns one or more
#                    of deploy-headless.sh / verify-deploy.sh / run-all.sh against a constructed
#                    or shared deployed tree). The boundary lint does not constrain these; Phase
#                    13's shared read-only deployed-tree fixture is scoped to this class.
#   reason     "-" for a unit-class suite. For an integration-class suite, "invokes:X[,Y,...]"
#              naming which of the three heavyweight tools (deploy-headless.sh, verify-deploy.sh,
#              run-all.sh) a literal textual reference to that tool's basename was found in the
#              suite's own content -- the same conservative, cheap, over-counting-never-under-
#              counting textual-reference method script-inventory.sh's own inbound_callers field
#              documents (a comment or fixture string mentioning the name also counts; a reader
#              auditing a specific row should open the file and confirm a real invocation).
#
# DERIVATION (re-run before trusting this file; the corpus drifts -- see script-inventory.sh's own
# header on the 30%-in-twelve-days finding):
#   grep -lE 'deploy-headless\.sh|verify-deploy\.sh|run-all\.sh' test-*.sh   # -> integration
#   every other discovered test-*.sh                                        # -> unit
#
# Classified 2026-11-05 against 157 suites discovered in the deployed, merged tests/ directory
# (139 physically filed under core, 18 under approvals/lean/literature -- see the SCOPE NOTE
# above; 116 unit, 41 integration).
